# Customer Segmentation
##  Objective
Segment customers using clustering.
## Approach
- Data Preprocessing
- Feature Scaling
- K-Means Clustering
## Insights
- 3 customer clusters identified
- High spenders vs low spenders
## Tools
- Python
- Scikit-learn

## Results & Insights
### 1. Customer Clusters Identified
Using K-Means clustering, customers were segmented into three distinct groups based on income and spending behavior. This segmentation helps in understanding different customer profiles.

### 2. High-Value Customers
One cluster represents high-income, high-spending customers. These customers contribute the most revenue and should be targeted with premium offerings and loyalty programs.

### 3. Budget-Conscious Customers
Another cluster includes low-income, low-spending customers. These customers are price-sensitive and respond better to discounts and promotional campaigns.

### 4. Potential Growth Segment
A middle cluster shows moderate income but high spending behavior. This segment has strong growth potential and can be converted into high-value customers with the right engagement strategies.

### 5. Business Recommendation
- Target high-value customers with personalized marketing
- Offer discounts to low-spending customers
- Upsell products to mid-tier customers
- Use segmentation for targeted campaigns instead of mass marketing
